     "line_end": 584,
     "label": "annex:p15.feller-polya-moments"
    }
   ],
   "gap": "State the positivity hypothesis on the red weight r > 0 for the Polya urn in thm:p15-feller-polya-moments (body handbook/parts/p15/feller-bernstein-hausdorff.tex lines 344-358; line 345 attaches positivity only to b and c). The identification of the mixing law with beta(b/c, r/c), used with Hausdorff uniqueness (annex lines 555-584), requires r > 0: beta(alpha,beta) is defined only for alpha,beta > 0 (def:p15-beta-integral) and thm:p15-polya-word-law assumes r > 0; at r = 0 the formula gives c_n = 1, the moments of delta_1, and no beta law exists. Either state r > 0 or treat r = 0 separately (mixing law delta_1)."
  }
